<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonld={jsonld} navVariant="inner">
<section class="hero">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow">Stage 2 — During production</span>
<h1>Catch it at 30% complete. Fix it in hours, not containers.</h1>
<p class="lead">The cheapest defect is the one caught mid-run. DUPRO inspects at 20–50% completion—components, early assemblies, first finished pieces—while rework costs hours, not containers.</p>
<div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-independent/">Why independent</a></div>
</div>
</section>
<section><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>What a during-production inspection checks</h2></div></div><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Moisture, before assembly hides it</h3><p>Core readings on components and panels—the point where a skipped kiln cycle is still fixable.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/#book"><h3>Dimensions &amp; first-offs</h3><p>First completed pieces measured against spec before the whole batch repeats an error.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/#book"><h3>Finish direction</h3><p>Early finished pieces vs golden sample, before 200 more are sprayed the wrong shade.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/production-monitoring-india/"><h3>Schedule truth</h3><p>Real progress vs claimed progress—the honest answer to "will it make the vessel?"</p></a></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>When to book DUPRO</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Book DUPRO at 20–50% completion—early enough that findings change the run, late enough that there is real product to inspect. On first orders and monsoon-season orders we recommend DUPRO plus PSI as a pair; the combination is included in the First Order Shield bundle. Same-day availability in Jodhpur and Jaipur, report within 24 hours, fixed fee from $249 published on booking.</p></div></section>
<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><div><h2>During-production inspection FAQ</h2></div></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details class="rv"><summary>When should a during-production inspection be booked?</summary><p>At 20–50% completion — early enough that findings still change the run, late enough that there is real product to inspect.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>What does DUPRO check that a pre-shipment inspection cannot?</summary><p>Core moisture readings on components and panels before assembly hides them, first-off dimensions before the batch repeats an error, and early finished pieces against the golden sample before the rest are sprayed.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>How much does a during-production inspection cost?</summary><p>From $249, with the fixed fee published on booking. The report follows within 24 hours of the visit.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>Should DUPRO be combined with a pre-shipment inspection?</summary><p>On first orders and monsoon-season orders we recommend DUPRO plus PSI as a pair. That combination is included in the <a href="/first-order-shield/">First Order Shield</a> bundle.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
